    "No default route synthesized; 0.0.0.0/32 is preserved unchanged.",
    "No default VRF synthesized; captured device has zero configured VPN instances.",
    "Virtual NE type comes from the documented GNS3 VSR lab deployment, not LLDP alone.",
    "No virtual node-to-inventory mapping claimed by reusing identical example keys.",
    "LLDP serial number is retained in capture; no invented physical component for the VM.",
    "Hub, unmanaged switches, IPv6, counters and physical wiring remain outside these subsets.",
    "ARP rows on VLAN interfaces are placed on the unique L3 interface whose captured subnet contains the neighbor; the physical port stays in evidence.",
    "LLDP remote-systems-data is keyed by time-mark (sysUpTime at change). CLI 'Update time' exceeds the 121 s TTL, so it is not a receive age, but it may be uptime-at-change or time-since-change; unverified, so no remote entries.",
    "MAC filtering entries need database-id and a bridge port number; the CLI shows an interface name only, so the MAC table is not synthesized.",
    "Bridge address is mandatory but not captured; bridge/component keys are projection labels; the l2 subsets therefore remain partial.",
    "Only the nearest-bridge LLDP agent is mapped; multi-line system description and management-address TLVs stay in evidence."
